<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-3"><summary><span class="chapter-count">03</span><h3>Full-Service Landscape Installation in Aurora, CO — From First Grade to Final Plant</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Landscape installation done well is a sequenced, technical process. The order of operations matters. Grading and drainage have to be right before anything else goes in. Irrigation needs to be installed before planting. Hardscape elements need proper base preparation before surface materials go down. Shortcut any of these steps and the problems show up later — settling patios, waterlogged beds, irrigation leaks, and plants that never fully establish.</p>
<p>Our installation teams have spent more than a decade working in Aurora and across the Denver metro. We know how Aurora’s soils behave — the clay content that retains water in the wrong places, the compaction that comes with new construction, the amendments needed to get planting beds to actually support plant growth. We design irrigation systems around Colorado’s evaporation rates and zone them properly for the plant types they serve.</p>
<p>As a full-service landscaping contractor in Aurora, we manage the complete installation scope: site grading and drainage, soil preparation and amendment, irrigation installation, sod or seeding, planting bed establishment, hardscape integration, and site cleanup. Every phase is handled by our team. Nothing is handed off mid-project to a subcontractor you’ve never met.</p>
<p>When we finish an installation, your landscape is ready — not waiting on someone else to complete the last piece.</p>

<h3>Custom Landscaping Services for Every Aurora Home and Property</h3>

<p>Aurora’s residential landscape needs vary as much as its neighbourhoods. Homes in the older parts of the city — established tree cover, compact lots, defined street character — need designs that work with what’s already there and improve it without overwhelming it. Newer developments in east Aurora and the southern suburbs often start with bare yards and open space that needs structure, planting, and definition to feel finished.</p>
<p>We design for all of it. Our approach starts with the specific property — its dimensions, existing features, sun exposure, drainage patterns, and how the homeowner uses the space — before a single design decision is made. From there we develop a landscape plan that fits the property and the person living in it.</p>
<p>That might be a refined front yard redesign focused on curb appeal and low maintenance. It might be a full backyard transformation with lawn, planting zones, a patio, and defined outdoor living areas. Or it might be a phased project where we design the full landscape upfront and build it in stages over one or two seasons — a practical approach for homeowners who want the complete picture without doing everything at once.</p>
<p>Whatever the scope, the design comes before the installation, and both come from the same team.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-4"><summary><span class="chapter-count">04</span><h3>Commercial Landscaping Services in Aurora for Properties That Make an Impression</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>For commercial properties in Aurora, landscaping is a business asset. A well-designed, well-maintained landscape signals professionalism, builds confidence with customers and tenants, and contributes to a property’s perceived value before anyone sets foot inside. A neglected or poorly designed landscape does the opposite — and in a competitive commercial environment, that first impression is hard to recover from.</p>
<p>Ridgewell provides commercial landscaping services in Aurora for businesses, property managers, HOAs, and commercial developers. Our commercial work focuses on the design and installation phase — creating landscapes that are functional, professionally presented, and built to be manageable long-term without demanding excessive maintenance resources.</p>
<p>We design commercial landscapes around the realities of commercial property management. Plant selection prioritises durability and low maintenance burden. Irrigation systems are zoned and specified to minimise ongoing adjustment. Hardscape elements — pathways, feature areas, entry treatments — are built for high foot traffic and long-term appearance. Every decision is made with the property’s operational requirements in mind, not just how it looks on day one.</p>
<p>We also understand that commercial projects operate differently from residential ones — tighter timelines, multiple stakeholders, site access constraints, and the need to keep business operations running during installation. Our process is structured to accommodate all of it.</p>
</div>
</details>
