<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-8"><summary><span class="chapter-count">08</span><h3>What Aurora Homeowners and Business Owners Ask Us Most About Landscaping Services</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><div class="content-feature">
<div id="eael-adv-accordion-c132f7d">
<div id="-how-much-do-landscaping-services-cost-in-aurora-co"><h3> How much do landscaping services cost in Aurora, CO?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2021"><p>Landscape project costs in Aurora vary based on scope, property size, and the combination of services involved. A focused front yard redesign with new planting, lawn, and edging typically starts around $5,000–$10,000. Full backyard landscape installations with irrigation, hardscape, and planting generally range from $15,000–$40,000. Larger commercial projects or full property transformations can exceed $50,000 depending on scale and complexity. We provide detailed, itemised quotes after an in-person site assessment — so you have a clear picture of what’s included and what it costs before any work begins.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-you-offer-commercial-landscaping-services-in-aurora"><h3>Do you offer commercial landscaping services in Aurora?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2022"><p>Yes. We provide commercial landscape design and installation for businesses, HOAs, property managers, and developers in Aurora. Our commercial service covers the full design and build scope — creating landscapes that look professional, perform reliably through Colorado’s seasons, and are practical to maintain long-term. We work with commercial clients who have specific timelines, stakeholder requirements, and site access constraints, and our process is structured to handle all of it.</p>
</div>

<div id="what-makes-ridgewell-a-full-service-landscaping-contractor-in-aurora-"><h3>What makes Ridgewell a full-service landscaping contractor in Aurora? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2023"><p>Full-service means we handle every phase of a landscape project with our own in-house team — design, permitting, site preparation, grading, irrigation installation, planting, hardscape, and final cleanup. You won’t have a designer from one company, an installer from another, and a plumber for the irrigation. One team manages the full scope, which eliminates the handoff problems that cause most landscape project failures and gives you a single accountable point of contact throughout.</p>
</div>

<div id="how-long-does-landscape-installation-take-in-aurora"><h3>How long does landscape installation take in Aurora?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2024"><p>Timeline depends on the scope of the project. A straightforward front yard refresh can be completed in a few days. A full backyard landscape installation with hardscape, irrigation, and comprehensive planting typically takes 2–4 weeks. Larger commercial installations or full property redesigns take longer. We provide a realistic project schedule before work starts and keep you updated throughout so you always know where things stand.</p>
</div>

<div id="can-you-handle-both-residential-and-commercial-landscaping-in-aurora"><h3>Can you handle both residential and commercial landscaping in Aurora?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2025"><p>Yes. We work with Aurora homeowners on residential landscape design and installation, and with businesses, property managers, and HOAs on commercial landscape projects. The design process and installation standards are the same across both — what changes is how we structure the project to suit the client’s context and requirements.</p>
</div>

<div id="-do-you-offer-phased-landscape-installation-for-aurora-homeowners"><h3> Do you offer phased landscape installation for Aurora homeowners?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2026"><p>Yes. Many Aurora homeowners want a complete landscape design but prefer to build it out over one or two seasons rather than all at once. We accommodate this by designing the full landscape upfront — so everything is planned cohesively — and then building it in agreed phases. This approach keeps the overall design consistent while spreading the investment across a more manageable timeline.</p>
</div>

<div id="can-you-handle-auroras-water-restrictions-in-your-landscape-designs-"><h3>Can you handle Aurora's water restrictions in your landscape designs? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2027"><p>Absolutely — and it’s something we plan for on every project. Aurora Water has specific irrigation requirements and seasonal watering schedules that all new landscape installations need to comply with. We design irrigation systems that work within those restrictions, and we actively recommend drought-tolerant and Colorado-native plant selections that perform well with reduced water input. A properly designed Aurora landscape should look great without exceeding your water budget or the city’s irrigation guidelines.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-you-design-landscapes-that-include-both-lawn-and-hardscape-elements-"><h3>Do you design landscapes that include both lawn and hardscape elements? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2028"><p>Yes, and integrating both from a single team is one of the biggest advantages of working with a full-service landscaping contractor. When lawn, planting, irrigation, and hardscape are all designed and installed together, the elements work as a system — drainage is accounted for, irrigation doesn’t conflict with hardscape, and the finished result has visual and functional cohesion that’s very difficult to achieve when multiple contractors are working from separate plans.</p>
</div>

